{"name":"A Stitch in Time","hex":"#babccf","fetched":"2026-10-16","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"a stitch in time","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Proverb","definitions":["A little effort expended sooner to fix a small problem prevents it from becoming a larger problem requiring more effort to fix later."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/a_stitch_in_time"}],"entries":[{"title":"A Stitch in Time (EP)","blocks":[{"text":"A Stitch in Time is the second EP released by The Twilight Singers. The five song EP was first released on iTunes on October 10, 2006. Hard copies were then released in the UK on December 4, 2006, and in the US on January 23, 2007. A Stitch in Time features guest appearances by Mark Lanegan and Joseph Arthur. \"Live with Me\" is a Massive Attack cover, while \"Flashback\" is a Fat Freddy's Drop cover."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/8/8b/A_stitch_in_time.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/A_Stitch_in_Time_(EP)","wikidata":"Q4659808"},{"title":"A Stitch in Time (Robinson novel)","blocks":[{"text":"A Stitch in Time is a Star Trek: Deep Space Nine novel written by Andrew Robinson. The novel originated from a biography of Cardassian Elim Garak in the form of a diary which was written by Robinson after he landed the recurring role in the series. He would read extracts from it at Star Trek conventions for fans, and was heard by novelist David R. George III, who suggested he should submit it for publishing. Although it was announced that a sequel would be published in 2001, co-written by fellow actor Alexander Siddig, the only follow-up to the novel was Robinson's short story The Calling which was published as part of the Prophecy and Change anthology in 2003."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/e/e5/Astitchintimecover.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/A_Stitch_in_Time_(Robinson_novel)","wikidata":"Q4659809"},{"title":"Time","blocks":[{"text":"Time is the continuous progression of existence that occurs in an apparently irreversible succession from the past, through the present, and into the future. Time dictates all forms of action, age, and causality, being a component quantity of various measurements used to sequence events, to compare the duration of events or the intervals between them, and to quantify rates of change of quantities in material reality or in conscious experience. Time is often referred to as the fourth dimension and the temporal dimension, in addition to the three spatial dimensions."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/45/MontreGousset001.jpg/330px-MontreGousset001.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Time","wikidata":"Q11471"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/8/8b/A_stitch_in_time.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled 1x","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/8/8b/A_stitch_in_time.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AA_stitch_in_time.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/e/e5/Astitchintimecover.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled 1x","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/e/e5/Astitchintimecover.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AAstitchintimecover.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/43/Andrew_Robinson.jpg/330px-Andrew_Robinson.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/43/Andrew_Robinson.jpg/330px-Andrew_Robinson.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Andrew Robinson became the first Star Trek actor to publish a Star Trek novel without another writer with A Stitch in Time.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AAndrew_Robinson.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/45/MontreGousset001.jpg/500px-MontreGousset001.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/45/MontreGousset001.jpg/500px-MontreGousset001.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AMontreGousset001.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/70/Wooden_hourglass_3.jpg/500px-Wooden_hourglass_3.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/70/Wooden_hourglass_3.jpg/500px-Wooden_hourglass_3.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"The flow of sand in an hourglass can be used to measure the passage of one hour of time. It also concretely represents the present as being between the past and the future.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AWooden_hourglass_3.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2a/Canberra_%28AU%29%2C_Albert_Hall%2C_Sundial_--_2019_--_1740.jpg/500px-Canberra_%28AU%29%2C_Albert_Hall%2C_Sundial_--_2019_--_1740.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2a/Canberra_%28AU%29%2C_Albert_Hall%2C_Sundial_--_2019_--_1740.jpg/1280px-Canberra_%28AU%29%2C_Albert_Hall%2C_Sundial_--_2019_--_1740.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2a/Canberra_%28AU